Subject: [PATCH 6/8] paper v2 (M9): the hardcopy package was rendered and
 degraded in simulation, not printed

NUMBERS.md 5.9 says nothing was ever printed and degrade.py is a model of
print-and-photograph. Three sentences in PAPER.md said otherwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 paper/v2/PAPER.md | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/paper/v2/PAPER.md b/paper/v2/PAPER.md
index 6a735b0..bcdfaa4 100644
--- a/paper/v2/PAPER.md
+++ b/paper/v2/PAPER.md
@@ -60,8 +60,8 @@ This paper’s central argument is that shaping a format *opposed* to that metri
 5. **`werk`**[^fn: The format's name is `werk` (German *Werk*: a work, an opus); files carry the extension `.werk`. The name is set in typewriter face throughout, to distinguish it from the ordinary German word. ^], a container doctrine whose acceptance gates are stated in terms of
    the metric and whose specification travels inside every file it describes
    (§2, §3), extended here to two artifact classes that stress it: an
-   **executable** payload carried as source (§5.7) and a **printed** package
-   whose only substrate is ink (§5.8).
+   **executable** payload carried as source (§5.7) and a **print-ready** package
+   whose only substrate is the page, here rendered and degraded in simulation (§5.8).
 6. **Ecosystem evidence that the metric is necessary but not sufficient**: seven
    consumers with re-runnable gates, including a self-regenerating package, a
    pixel-identical cross-engine texture round trip, and a prose-specified digest
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@ against the real package and feeds back the traceback; the bundled loaders are
 never inlined, because pasting them in would make the loader metric meaningless.
 The **self-run arm** changes the artifact rather than the implementer — the
 payload is *executable*, and the task is to run it — and the **hardcopy arm**
-changes the substrate, printing the package and handing the reader photographs.
+changes the substrate, rendering the package as pages and handing the reader simulated photographs of them.
 
 The seven runs, in order. Round 1 ran four agents in Python, JavaScript, Rust and C against a 3D-entity package. Round 2 ran two agents in Python and Rust against an image package carrying a custom binary payload, chosen to close the gap round 1's own verdict identified: round 1's fixture had no custom binary at all, so the entire envelope apparatus went untested. Round 3, the mini-gauntlet, ran one agent against the Gaussian-splat package, with an explicit additional instruction not to execute anything that came out of the file. Round 4, the cross-vendor round, gave two other laboratories' frontier models round 1's task sentence verbatim and then round 3's, on the pinned committed fixtures. Round 5, the open-weights round, is the void arm, with a post-fix second arm that re-ran the failing models after their findings had been turned into specification text. Round 6, the self-run round, handed out a package carrying a language model and its runtime's source. Round 7, the hardcopy round, handed out three photographs.
 
@@ -826,7 +826,7 @@ payload bytes per module net of parity against QR version 40-L's 0.09426, the
